course: dictionary
lesson: 9715
title: The Sumerians
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sumer was one of the world's first civilisations, with cities, writing and rules, about 5,000 years ago in southern Mesopotamia, which is now southern Iraq. A Sumerian is a person from Sumer. Sumerian can also describe things from Sumer, such as its language. «The Sumerians counted in groups of sixty, which is why we still have 60 seconds in a minute.» Here Sumerians means the people of Sumer.
explain: Use the context to check. «So the Sumerians invented writing, first as little pictures of grain and sheep.» The word invented tells you people made writing for the first time, so Sumerians must be the people who made it. Try the check: swap in «people from Sumer» and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Sumerian is an adjective when it sits before a noun, like «Sumerian cities» or «Sumerian writing». Then it describes the thing, not the people. Look at the word next to it to see which job it is doing.
fact: Sumerian means from or to do with Sumer, a very early civilisation in southern Mesopotamia (now southern Iraq).
fact: A Sumerian is a person from Sumer.
fact: Sumerian is also the language the Sumerians spoke, written in cuneiform.
fact: Cuneiform was pressed into wet clay with a reed, and it is one of the oldest written languages.
fact: The Sumerians used a number system based on 60, which is why we have 60 minutes in an hour.
exercise: «The Sumerians built some of the first cities, like Ur and Uruk.» What is a Sumerian? | A type of reed used for writing | A king of ancient Egypt | *A person from Sumer | A number from one to ten
exercise: «The Sumerians counted in groups of sixty.» Find and copy one word that means the people of Sumer. | counted | *Sumerians | groups | sixty
exercise: What was the Sumerian language written in? | Pictures painted on cave walls | Hieroglyphs | Latin letters | *Cuneiform
test: In «Sumerian cities», what kind of word is Sumerian? | Noun | *Adjective | Pronoun | Verb
test: «The Sumerians pressed a reed into wet clay.» What did they press the reed into to write? | *Wet clay | Paper | Stone | Sand
exam: Which best describes a Sumerian? | *A person from Sumer, one of the first civilisations | A kind of stepped temple | A modern city in Iraq | A type of writing made of pictures
